Done. Added three tests to `test/unit/repository_test.dart` in the existing `SettingsRepository` group:

- `readThemeMode returns actual value after initAsyncData` — stubs `mockPreferenceDatasource.themeMode`, calls `initAsyncData()`, then asserts `readThemeMode()` returns the actual value (`AppThemeMode.dark`) and that the datasource getter was read once.
- `readThemeMode reads the updated value after setThemeMode` — verifies `readThemeMode()` reflects a change made via `setThemeMode()` (light → system).
- `readThemeMode is safe only after initAsyncData` — asserts the call happens after `initAsyncData()` and returns normally (`returnsNormally`), matching the project convention in `docs/migration-v2.md` §3 that `readThemeMode()` is only valid post-Splash initialization.

No production code was modified; the tests use the existing `MockPreferenceDatasource` and the non-deprecated `readThemeMode()` API.

